## Skin care

- wash the affected areas **twice a day** with a mild soap or cleanser and lukewarm water
- do not scrub, as this can make acne worse
- use **non-comedogenic** (will not block pores) moisturisers, make-up and sun cream
- take make-up off before bed

## Do not pick or squeeze

Picking spots can cause infection and **scarring**.

## Stick with treatment

Most treatments take **6 to 8 weeks** to start working, and acne can seem worse at first. Keep going unless your GP says otherwise.

## Your mental health

Skin conditions can affect confidence, relationships and mood. Anxiety and depression are more common in people with long-term skin conditions. Talk to your GP if you are struggling. You can refer yourself to **NHS Talking Therapies** in England. **Changing Faces** supports people with a visible difference.

## Support

The **British Skin Foundation** has information about acne.
